/// What an application of examples/ declares about itself: `examples/<name>/app.pkl` amends
/// this module (examples/AGENTS.md). The lanes' work (tools/ci/work.py) reads it as the
/// pinned Pkl CLI evaluates it (tools/pkl/evaluate.py), with the defaults and types below.
module App

typealias Lane = "desktop" | "source-engine" | "android" | "ios"

/// The lanes that verify the application: `desktop` and `source-engine` run its own tests,
/// `android` and `ios` build its release apps with their debug symbols, for every Android
/// ABI.
lanes: List<Lane>(!isEmpty, isDistinct)

/// The Bazel configuration every command of the application takes, such as one that
/// registers its source-built engine.
config: String? = null
